# Open-String Duet (repertoire plan: st-open-string-duet). An original study in E minor.
# Your part: only the open strings 6, 5 and 4, in half and quarter notes. Bars 1-4 open E, bars
# 5-8 open A, bars 9-12 open D, bars 13-16 E, A, D, E. Each open string is the root of the
# teacher's chord (Em, Am, D), so your note is always the bottom of the harmony.
# The teacher's tune has the same shape over each chord: up the chord, down by step, a turn, a
# landing. The last four bars bring the three chords together and come home to E.
title: Open-String Duet
id: st-open-string-duet
composer: Sixstring Academy
source: Original duet study for Sixstring Academy
